# Input for requirements-semgrep.txt (the pinned, hash-checked Semgrep install of .github/workflows/semgrep.yml).
# The lockfile is for linux x86_64 and Python 3.12 only (the CI runner); it has no autogenerated header on purpose.
# Regenerate it from the repository root (relative paths below), in a linux container, with the command that made it:
#   docker run --rm -v "$PWD":/w -w /w python:3.12-slim sh -c "pip install uv==0.13.8 && uv pip compile requirements-semgrep.in --exclude-newer 2026-11-12 --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_34 --python-version 3.12 --generate-hashes --no-header -o requirements-semgrep.txt"
# --exclude-newer 2026-11-12 is the day of the first lock run: it stops later releases of the other packages from moving the lock.
# Re-run on 2026-11-12 with uv 0.13.8 (pip-installed from PyPI into a scratch venv under Python 3.13, run directly, not through the
# docker command above; same arguments): `cmp` found the regenerated file byte-identical to this one (sha256 starting a791abb7e447d8db..., 1130 lines). The docker command itself was not run (no docker there).
# To bump Semgrep: change the pin below, set --exclude-newer to today's date, rerun, READ the lock diff (every package may move),
# run `python -m pytest tests/test_hygiene.py -q` (new package names or hashes may need a line in exceptions.txt),
# then read the first scan result (docs/tests.md, "Semgrep": status of the scan).
# This lock needs the gitleaks `cwd=target` change in tests/test_hygiene.py (the scan runs from the repository root) to be in place first.
# Who bumps: the repository owner, when a Semgrep security advisory appears or about once a quarter.
# Dependabot does NOT cover this file (.github/dependabot.yml asks for GitHub Actions only).
semgrep==1.185.0
